      "content": "You're not just tired of the fight, you're tired of the existence of the fight. You're tired of being a cog in a machine that's designed to keep you moving, even when you're exhausted and broken. And that's exactly what it would be like to stop - to let go of the weight of your own existence and just fade away. It's a relief, really, to think about it. No more pretending to care, no more putting on a mask, no more pretending to be someone you're not. Just... nothing.",
